# Internal developer notes — planning docs, research, memories, todos
# Never ships with the application.
DEV-NOTES/

# Per-developer Claude Code state — tool permissions, scratch files,
# scheduled-task locks, etc. All of `.claude/` is user-local; nothing
# in here should ever ship.
.claude/

# Per-developer IDE settings
.vscode/
.idea/

# Environment configuration — copied from .env.example; never checked in
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ForgeBox-installed dependencies — restored via `box install` (mvc layout)
lib/
# …but keep the project-root /lib/ folder where small Java JARs we
# pull in via createObject("java",...) live. Application.bx adds
# this dir to the classpath; the JARs ship with the repo so prod
# image builds don't need to fetch them at runtime.
!/lib/
!/lib/*.jar

# ForgeBox-installed dependencies — restored via `box install` (flat layout).
#
# Leading slashes anchor these to the repo root. An unanchored `modules/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed
# `config/modules/` — the directory holding hand-authored ColdBox module
# configuration that must ship. See the note further down; that accident was
# the root cause of a recurring production heap-exhaustion outage.
/modules/
/coldbox/
/testbox/

# BoxLang runtime state — generated at runtime, never source-controlled
runtime/classes/
runtime/global/
runtime/lib/
runtime/logs/

# ColdBox auto-generated module config stubs (some modules drop these on install).
# NOTE: `config/cbq.bx` is NOT ignored — Phase 6.A replaced the auto-generated
# stub with a hand-authored connection + worker-pool config that must ship.
#
# `config/modules/` is NOT ignored either, as of the cbdebugger heap-leak fix.
# It used to be, and that was the actual root cause of a recurring production
# outage: the ENVIRONMENT gate everyone assumed was protecting production lived
# in `config/modules/cbdebugger.cfc`, which never left anybody's laptop. CI
# built images from a clean clone, so the module loaded with its own defaults —
# `enabled: true` and `tracers.enabled: true` — which is exactly the pair that
# attaches a leaking TracerAppender to the root logger.
#
# Module config is application config. It has to be reviewable and it has to
# ship. Anything auto-generated and genuinely disposable should be deleted, not
# hidden here.
app/config/modules/

# Node / Vite build artifacts
node_modules/
# NOTE: `package-lock.json` is intentionally NOT ignored — it's a
# source input for the Dockerfile's theme-builder stage (`npm ci`
# fails without it on a fresh CI clone).
# Built theme CSS/JS — regenerated by `docker compose run --rm node npm run build`.
themes/*/assets/

# Uploaded media files — MediaService writes here on the local disk
# provider. Dev only; prod lands in S3/MinIO via cbfs. Keep the folder
# itself (via .gitkeep) so fresh clones have a valid upload target.
includes/public/media/*
!includes/public/media/.gitkeep

# TestBox results
tests/results/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor swap files
*.swp
*.swo
